WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.400
Analysis turns artifacts into a defensible explanation.

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:14.820
Android activity timelines combine device data, app data, cloud data, messages, media, location, network logs, endpoint telemetry, and witness statements where available.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:18.880
The goal is not to dump every artifact into chronological order.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:25.340
The goal is to show the relevant sequence of events with enough context that another qualified person can understand the reasoning.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:29.080
Timestamp handling is one of the most important analysis skills.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:34.020
Different artifacts may use different formats, time zones, precision levels, and meanings.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:42.960
A created time, modified time, database insertion time, last accessed time, server time, and sync time may all point to different events.

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:48.220
Analysts should normalize carefully and preserve the original values where appropriate.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.360
Deleted data has limits.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:58.100
Some artifacts may remain in databases, caches, thumbnails, backups, or cloud records, while other data may be gone or inaccessible.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:05.760
Investigators should avoid implying that absence proves nonexistence unless the acquisition and artifact behavior support that conclusion.

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:09.820
A defensible report explains what the evidence can show and what it cannot show.

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:12.040
Tool output must be validated.

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:20.420
Forensic tools can parse artifacts differently, omit context, display derived fields, or make assumptions about timestamps and app behavior.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:30.400
Validation can include reviewing source files, comparing multiple artifacts, checking known formats, correlating with external logs, and documenting tool versions and methods.

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:34.380
The tool is an aid to analysis, not the authority by itself.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:37.400
Good reports separate observations from conclusions.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:43.620
An observation might say a record exists in a specific database with a specific timestamp and field value.

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:48.320
A conclusion explains what that likely means, with caveats and correlation.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:57.660
Privacy-aware reporting includes relevant evidence, avoids unnecessary personal data, documents methods and assumptions, and states uncertainty plainly.
